.TH MANAGE.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-runlog-db t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
manage.py \- Django management entry point of mu2edaq-runlog-db
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B .venv/bin/python manage.py
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B .venv/bin/python manage.py seed_db
.RB [ \-\-runs
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-subruns\-per\-run
.IR M ]
.RB [ \-\-start\-run
.IR R ]
.br
.B .venv/bin/python manage.py purge_db
.RB [ \-\-confirm ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standard Django
.B manage.py
with
.B DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=runlogdb.settings
as the default.
Settings are resolved as described in
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5);
in particular
.B DJANGO_ENV
(default
.BR development )
selects SQLite or PostgreSQL.
.B Every subcommand acts on whatever database that resolves to, including
.B the production run log.
.PP
The package adds two subcommands.
.TP
.B seed_db
Creates lookup rows
.RB ( run_type
ids 1\(en5,
.B run_transition_type
ids 1\(en4,
.B run_transition_cause
ids 1\(en4, by
.BR get_or_create )
and then, for each of
.I N
runs starting at
.IR R ,
a
.B run
row with an explicit run number, a
.B run_end_info
row, two
.B run_transition
rows, 2\(en5
.B config
rows and
.I M
.B subrun
rows with random event counts and EWT ranges.
Existing run numbers are skipped.
All inside one transaction.
.TP
.B purge_db
Deletes every row from
.BR artdaq_fcl ,
.BR config ,
.BR run_transition ,
.BR subrun ,
.BR run_end_info ,
.BR run ,
.BR run_type ,
.B run_transition_type
and
.BR run_transition_cause ,
in that order, in one transaction.
It first prints the row count and asks for
.BR yes .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-runs " N"
seed_db: number of runs (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-subruns\-per\-run " M"
seed_db: subruns per run (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-start\-run " R"
seed_db: first run number (default 1001).
.TP
.B \-\-confirm
purge_db: skip the
.B yes
prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR DJANGO_ENV ,
.BR DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE ,
and the
.B RUNLOGDB_*
variables of
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, including when
.B purge_db
is aborted at the prompt or finds nothing to delete.
Non-zero on a Django
.B CommandError
or an uncaught exception.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
DJANGO_ENV=development .venv/bin/python manage.py seed_db \-\-runs 5
DJANGO_ENV=development .venv/bin/python manage.py purge_db
DJANGO_ENV=development .venv/bin/python manage.py shell
.fi
.RE
.SH CAVEATS
Neither command checks the backend.
With
.B DJANGO_ENV=production
.B purge_db
deletes the production run log, including the rows written by the DAQ's
.B DBRunInfo
plugin, and
.B seed_db
inserts fake runs with explicit run numbers that the database sequence does
not know about, so a later DAQ run start can fail with a duplicate key.
Check
.B DJANGO_ENV
before running either.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
